# UML Artifact Standards

- Keep diagram source readable and logically grouped.
- Add a short title and a clear purpose where the notation/tool supports it.
- Do not hide modeling errors behind styling.
- Keep names consistent with the project vocabulary.
- Avoid unnecessary colors, icons, or layout tricks.
- For PlantUML, prefer stable constructs over obscure syntax.
- If a diagram becomes too large, split it by concern/use case rather than shrinking everything.
